cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Quantum Computing for Experienced Developers: A Structured Guide from Core
  Principles to Modern Practice
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: book
authors:
  - family-names: Voitovych
    given-names: Iaroslav
    email: yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A rigorous, engineering-oriented guide to quantum computing for experienced
  developers and technically mature readers: from core principles and the
  mathematical formalism through qubits, gates, circuits, measurement,
  algorithms, complexity, noise and error correction, hardware, tooling, and
  the modern algorithmic frontier, with explicit guidance on judging claims.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum algorithms
  - quantum error correction
  - quantum information
  - software engineering
